{
  "title": "Replace hand-written iOS API client (RamekinAPI.swift) with the \
generated client",
  "description": "iOS has two API layers: the generated client \
(ramekin-ios/generated-client/) and a ~460-line hand-written one \
(ramekin-ios/Shared/RamekinAPI.swift) used for login, HTML capture, scrape \
status, connection test, and ALL meal plan calls — with hand-rolled request \
structs like CreateMealPlanRequestBody that duplicate OpenAPI models.\n\
\n\
Every endpoint behind the hand-written layer is invisible to the codegen \
pipeline and can silently drift from the spec. This is a standing structural \
cause of iOS/web divergence.\n\
\n\
Migrate RamekinAPI.swift's endpoint calls onto the generated client, keeping \
only what genuinely can't be generated (auth/header plumbing like \
applyAccessHeaders and updateGeneratedClientConfig, server URL normalization, \
the share-extension-friendly surface). Delete the duplicated request/response \
structs. Mind the share extension: Shared/ is used from the extension target, \
so whatever remains must still work there.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "parity",
    "architecture",
  ],
